course: dictionary
lesson: 4525
title: Clothes that show who we are
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A headscarf is a piece of cloth worn over the head. It is often tied under the chin or at the back, and it covers the hair. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they give clues: «Religious clothing like a headscarf, turban or kippah is important to the people who wear it.»
explain: People wear headscarves for different reasons. Some keep warm, some wear them for fashion, some protect their head from the sun, and some wear them for religious reasons. «Many Muslim women and girls wear a hijab, a kind of headscarf.»
explain: The last part of that sentence is the key clue: important to the people who wear it. A headscarf matters to the person wearing it, so we treat it as normal. Mocking it is not fair. «Mocking someone's religion or clothes, like a headscarf, is bullying.»
fact: A headscarf is a piece of cloth worn over the head to cover the hair.
fact: Headscarves can be tied under the chin or at the back.
fact: People wear headscarves for warmth, fashion, sun protection or religious reasons.
fact: A hijab is a kind of headscarf worn by many Muslim women and girls.
fact: «Mocking» someone's clothes, like a headscarf, is bullying.
exercise: What is a headscarf? | A wide-brimmed hat worn on the beach | A kind of shoe worn for running | *A piece of cloth worn over the head to cover the hair | A scarf worn around the neck
exercise: «Religious clothing like a headscarf, turban or kippah is important to the people who wear it.» What should we do about it? | Ask people to take it off | Laugh at it when we see it | Hide it from our friends | *Treat it as normal and respect it
exercise: Which is a reason someone might wear a headscarf? | To swim faster in the pool | To make their hair wet | *To keep the sun off their head | To make a noise when they walk
test: What is a hijab? | A kind of shoe worn for football | *A kind of headscarf worn by many Muslim women and girls | A kind of hat for the rain | A type of bag for school books
test: «Mocking someone's religion or clothes, like a headscarf, is bullying.» What does this tell us? | Headscarves are only for cold weather | *Making fun of someone's headscarf is bullying | People should laugh at clothes they don't like | Teasing is fine if it is only a joke
exam: «A boy in Arizona made fun of a classmate's hijab every day; the girl became afraid to come to school.» What does the story show? | Hijabs are unsafe to wear to school | Teasing is a good way to make friends | *Mocking someone's headscarf can hurt them and is bullying | The girl should wear a different hat
